---
title: Turdidae
---
# Turdidae

Turdidae is the thrush family, medium-sized songbirds with a strong musical
voice and a broadly omnivorous diet. Most species build a substantial cup nest
of grass and dead leaves, many of them strengthening it with a lining of mud.
They feed on worms, insects and fruit, and take much of their food from the
ground. See [[common-blackbird]] and [[european-robin]].
